7. It’s important to consider the limitations of descriptive statistics. Give an example of a variable for which the mean alone would be unhelpful or misleading. Do the same for the median and mode.

   Answer: The mean could be misleading if there are outliers. A mean with outliers at the upper end of the distribution may not match the point where most of the data clusters. 
   The median would be unhelpful to capture a “typical” member of the dataset if it had a bimodal distribution. 
   The mode would be unhelpful for continuous data that was measured with a high enough level of precision such that it's rare for values to be repeated. There may not even be a mode. For example, temperature readings that are measured in Celsius to 4 decimal places.

